.* QDSIGNON: the help of the sign-on display, display files QSYS/QDSIGNON
.* and QDSIGNON2 (ui/dspf/sys/). Their help specifications name these
.* modules; the telnet server shows them when Help or F1 is pressed.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:HELP NAME=SIGNON.Sign On
:P.The sign-on display starts an interactive job at this display. Type
your user profile and password and press Enter. The other fields are
optional: they override, for this job only, what your user profile
says the job starts with.
:P.The upper right shows the system, the subsystem that will run the
job and the name of the display device.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SIGNON/USER'.User
:P.Your user profile name, up to 10 characters. Ask your security
officer for one if you have none.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SIGNON/PWD'.Password
:P.The password of the user profile. It is not shown as you type it.
Passwords are case sensitive when the system allows mixed-case
passwords. After too many wrong passwords the profile is disabled, as
the system value QMAXSIGN says.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SIGNON/PROGRAM'.Program/procedure
:P.A program to call when the job starts, in place of the initial
program of your user profile. Leave it blank to use the profile's.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SIGNON/MENU'.Menu
:P.The menu to show when the job starts, in place of the initial menu
of your user profile. Leave it blank to use the profile's.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='SIGNON/CURLIB'.Current library
:P.The current library of the job, in place of the one your user
profile names. Leave it blank to use the profile's.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
